msgid "What this site is"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An automatically updated tracker of cyber attack activity related to the "
"People's Republic of China, in both directions: campaigns by China-"
"attributed threat actors, and attacks against targets inside China. It is"
" a personal research tool; nothing here is original attribution research."
msgstr ""

msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

msgid "Fetch"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the pipeline pulls the latest articles from public security sources "
"(vendor research blogs, government advisories, security news) via RSS, in"
" English and Chinese."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"articles are pre-screened by keywords: the names and aliases of China-"
"attributed groups imported from MITRE ATT&CK, plus geographic terms. "
"Matching articles become candidates."
msgstr ""

msgid "Filter"
msgstr ""

msgid "Extract"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"each candidate article is read by an LLM, which records every attack it "
"describes in a fixed schema: actor, victim country and sector, date, "
"direction, MITRE ATT&CK techniques, and a confidence level. Malformed "
"answers are rejected, and irrelevant articles yield no incidents."
msgstr ""

msgid "Publish"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the database is rendered into this static site in three languages. Every "
"incident links back to the article it came from."
msgstr ""

